@startuml sequence-check-availability
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
hide footbox
title Sequence — Check availability (UC4a, included in UC4 and UC8)

box "Caller (UC4 or UC8)" #FFF3E0
  participant "caller\n(:CarsRouter, :ReservationsRouter\nor :ReservationService)" as Caller
end box
box "Services" #E8F5E9
  participant ":ReservationService" as ResService
end box
box "Persistence" #F3E5F5
  participant "db : Session" as DB
end box

note over Caller
  Called from three places:
  1. CarsRouter.check_availability — live check while the
     customer picks dates (UC4)
  2. ReservationsRouter.create_reservation — right before a
     reservation is created (UC4)
  3. ReservationService.confirm_reservation — right before
     the admin confirms a reservation (UC8)
end note

Caller -> ResService : is_car_available(car_id, start_date, end_date)
ResService -> DB : query(Reservation).filter(\n  car_id == car_id,\n  status == CONFIRMED,\n  start_date < requested end_date,\n  end_date > requested start_date\n).first()
note right of DB
  DRAFT and CANCELLED
  reservations are ignored —
  only a CONFIRMED one
  blocks the slot
end note
DB --> ResService : overlapping : Reservation | None

alt overlapping is None
  ResService --> Caller : true (car available)
else an overlapping CONFIRMED reservation exists
  ResService --> Caller : false (car not available)
end

note over Caller
  What the caller does with the result:
  • check_availability → 200 OK {available: true / false}
  • create_reservation → false means 409 Conflict
  • confirm_reservation → false raises DomainError → 409 Conflict
end note
@enduml
